that fact upon my heart.

00:15:59.950 --> 00:16:01.160
How silly of you.

00:16:01.160 --> 00:16:02.950
You don't need to think of me.

00:16:03.320 --> 00:16:05.090
I'm family, after all.

00:16:07.960 --> 00:16:12.460
Yumi-san, Sayako Oba-sama said
she'll make us matcha green tea later.

00:16:13.130 --> 00:16:14.430
Let's be quick and clean things up.

00:16:15.000 --> 00:16:15.800
Okay.

00:16:19.410 --> 00:16:20.270
Give me all the trash.

00:16:20.340 --> 00:16:21.430
What fun!

00:16:24.280 --> 00:16:25.250
What fun!

00:16:28.220 --> 00:16:29.270
This is delicious.

00:16:29.980 --> 00:16:31.780
I am so happy.

00:16:36.360 --> 00:16:42.850
But for some reason, I feel a cold
breeze stealing into my heart...

00:16:43.830 --> 00:16:45.300
That's probably because...

00:16:45.300 --> 00:16:47.730
...you're storing your emotions
in the wrong room.

00:16:47.900 --> 00:16:50.430
Huh? Did I just say something?

00:16:50.900 --> 00:16:51.630
Yes.

00:16:51.870 --> 00:16:55.310
That you are happy, but a cold
breeze is coming into your heart,

00:16:55.310 --> 00:16:56.470
or something to that effect.

00:16:57.440 --> 00:16:58.670
I must have it bad!

00:16:58.880 --> 00:17:00.280
The two of you are right next to me...

00:17:00.280 --> 00:17:02.340
...and I'm babbling my thoughts out loud!

00:17:02.520 --> 00:17:03.710
It can't be helped.

00:17:03.920 --> 00:17:07.520
Even when your "big sister's room"
and your "friends' rooms" are full,

00:17:07.520 --> 00:17:09.660
when another room is empty,

00:17:09.660 --> 00:17:12.150
you might feel like you're missing something.

00:17:12.230 --> 00:17:13.720
What "other room"?

00:17:13.790 --> 00:17:15.160
Your "little sister's room."

00:17:15.230 --> 00:17:16.700
There is no such room.

00:17:16.700 --> 00:17:17.990
Not before now.

00:17:18.530 --> 00:17:21.630
But you built a new room
for Toko-chan, didn't you?

00:17:21.800 --> 00:17:22.700
Recently.

00:17:24.370 --> 00:17:26.470
You built the room in advance,

00:17:26.470 --> 00:17:28.410
but you have no little sister to live there,

00:17:28.410 --> 00:17:32.070
and that's why you have a draft
blowing through your heart.

00:17:33.950 --> 00:17:36.140
So it's only to be expected.

00:17:36.820 --> 00:17:38.050
Just stand firm and say,

00:17:38.050 --> 00:17:40.890
"That's just how it is. What's wrong with that?"

00:17:41.590 --> 00:17:42.990
What a nice way to put it.

00:17:44.090 --> 00:17:45.290
Shimako-san...

00:17:47.800 --> 00:17:49.930
After all, as the one saying these words,

00:17:49.930 --> 00:17:52.500
I'm also in the midst of
building a new room myself.

00:17:52.500 --> 00:17:53.560
I see...

00:17:57.810 --> 00:17:59.770
A person's heart is a house, huh?

00:18:00.870 --> 00:18:03.370
When I think of it that way,
it's easy to understand.

00:18:03.440 --> 00:18:06.410
And the room for my dear sister and I...

00:18:06.410 --> 00:18:08.510
...is already filled to the point of bursting.

00:18:10.280 --> 00:18:13.650
Now, we definitely have to write
that up before going to sleep!

00:18:14.090 --> 00:18:15.150
That?

00:18:15.260 --> 00:18:16.350
"Upon the Long Night."

00:18:16.520 --> 00:18:18.930
You write a palindrome poem that
starts with "Upon the Long Night,"

00:18:18.930 --> 00:18:20.890
and you sleep with it under your pillow.

00:18:21.230 --> 00:18:23.760
It's a charm for making the first
dream of the year a pleasant one.

00:18:23.760 --> 00:18:26.160
I'm impressed that you remembered, Yumi.

00:18:27.630 --> 00:18:29.600
Upon the long night,
from the depths of sound slumber,
all awaken now, the good fortune treasure ship,
sounds so fine upon the waves.

00:18:35.540 --> 00:18:37.340
Then I'm going to turn out the lights.

00:18:37.850 --> 00:18:39.040
Good night.
Good night.

00:18:55.160 --> 00:18:57.560
She looks so adorable in her sleep.

00:18:58.900 --> 00:19:02.730
I feel so much for her and she's
just my friend's little sister.

00:19:03.640 --> 00:19:07.630
If this were my own little sister...

00:19:16.450 --> 00:19:18.780
My first dream of the year was...

00:19:19.720 --> 00:19:22.420
...predictably, a dream about Toko-chan.

00:19:31.630 --> 00:19:34.290
Toko-chan is in the room next to mine.

00:19:35.300 --> 00:19:39.900
But there is a clouded pane
of glass separating us.

00:19:40.640 --> 00:19:42.630
I want to see Toko-chan's face...

00:19:47.950 --> 00:19:51.110
Please, Toko-chan! Wipe it from your side, too!

00:19:52.120 --> 00:19:54.680
Or this cloud won't clear away!

00:19:55.520 --> 00:19:57.350
Yumi-san, what are you doing?

00:19:57.720 --> 00:19:59.620
Oh, no, nothing.

00:20:00.090 --> 00:20:01.260
Oh, look at this!

00:20:01.260 --> 00:20:02.000
What did I do wrong?
Oh, look at this!

00:20:02.000 --> 00:20:03.190
What did I do wrong?

00:20:03.630 --> 00:20:05.830
What can I do to make her understand?

00:20:06.470 --> 00:20:08.300
Toko-chan, please!

00:20:08.970 --> 00:20:10.300
Look this way!

00:20:29.920 --> 00:20:31.190
Toko-chan...

00:20:37.360 --> 00:20:40.230
Thank you very much for inviting us.

00:20:40.530 --> 00:20:42.530
We had a lot of fun!

00:20:43.000 --> 00:20:44.500
Please come again.

00:20:44.500 --> 00:20:45.470
Good-bye.

00:20:46.010 --> 00:20:47.300
Good-bye.
Good-bye.

00:20:57.150 --> 00:20:58.810
I want to see Toko-chan.

00:20:59.420 --> 00:21:01.390
I want to make Toko-chan my little sister.

00:21:02.160 --> 00:21:04.650
I want to know everything about Toko-chan.

00:21:08.100 --> 00:21:11.900
Maybe I'll try dropping by
Kashiwagi-san's place...

00:21:16.570 --> 00:21:21.530
If I ask Kashiwagi-san, I may be
able to learn more about Toko-chan.

00:21:22.840 --> 00:21:27.540
But, Toko-chan may not be pleased if I do that.

00:21:27.810 --> 00:21:30.510
In fact, she might close
her heart to me even more.

00:21:32.390 --> 00:21:34.510
I mustn't do such a thing.

00:21:34.820 --> 00:21:36.620
That's not how a big sister behaves.

00:21:40.090 --> 00:21:43.120
I'm not worthy of being called "Onee-sama."

00:21:53.210 --> 00:21:56.540
Unable to do anything,
the new school term started.

00:22:03.720 --> 00:22:04.740
Toko-chan...

00:22:14.660 --> 00:22:16.360
Good morning, Yumi-sama.

00:22:16.960 --> 00:22:18.620
G-Good morning.

00:22:20.800 --> 00:22:22.630
Toko-chan is smiling...

00:22:23.370 --> 00:22:25.240
As if what happened last year...

00:22:25.240 --> 00:22:27.570
As if what happened between us...

00:22:27.570 --> 00:22:29.540
...never happened at all.

00:22:30.410 --> 00:22:33.540
As if she's forgotten about it all.

00:22:44.730 --> 00:22:47.790
A winterscape where even...
Machi no irodori sae doko

00:22:47.790 --> 00:22:52.360
...the town's colors seem forlorn somehow
to naku samishige na fuyu no keshiki

00:22:52.730 --> 00:22:56.540
I think of you, turning your back on me...
Senaka mise kaketeitta

00:22:56.540 --> 00:23:00.270
...and running off
anata o omou

00:23:01.240 --> 00:23:05.280
There's a clear square pane...
Futari no aida ni wa

00:23:05.280 --> 00:23:09.280
...between the two of us
toumei na shikakkei

00:23:09.280 --> 00:23:12.020
It's misted over right now...
Ima wa kasunderu

00:23:12.020 --> 00:23:18.620
...with the crystals of sighs
tame-iki no kesshou de

00:23:19.230 --> 00:23:23.300
Window glass, window glass
Mado garasu mado garasu

00:23:23.300 --> 00:23:29.240
It's clouded and I can't see you
Kumottete anata ga mienai no

00:23:29.240 --> 00:23:35.140
Even though I know that you're there
Soko ni iru koto wa wakatteiru no ni

00:23:35.280 --> 00:23:39.180
Are you smiling? Are you crying?
Waratteru naiteru no

00:23:39.180 --> 00:23:45.080
I don't even care if you're frowning, let me see you
Shikamettsura demo ii kara misete

00:23:45.190 --> 00:23:53.650
Wipe the glass from your side, too
Sochira no hou kara mo garasu o fuite

00:24:06.010 --> 00:24:07.110
Preview

00:24:07.110 --> 00:24:09.410
Preview
Rei-chan, don't ever let go, okay?!

00:24:09.410 --> 00:24:10.540
Preview
I know.

00:24:10.540 --> 00:24:10.940
Preview

00:24:10.940 --> 00:24:15.250
Preview
That was how Rei-chan responded
when I was learning to ride a bicycle,

00:24:15.250 --> 00:24:18.050
Preview
but with flawless timing, she let go.

00:24:18.050 --> 00:24:18.290
Preview

00:24:18.290 --> 00:24:19.820
Preview
That was during winter break,

00:24:19.820 --> 00:24:23.160
Preview
after Nana and Rei-chan
finished their kendo match.

00:24:23.160 --> 00:24:25.460
Preview
You were cheering for Nana, weren't you?

00:24:25.460 --> 00:24:26.490
Preview
"That's how it should be," said Rei-chan.

00:24:26.490 --> 00:24:28.230
Preview
"That's how it should be," said Rei-chan.
The Masked Actress

00:24:28.230 --> 00:24:28.530
Preview
The Masked Actress

00:24:28.530 --> 00:24:30.700
Preview
Next time, "The Masked Actress."
The Masked Actress

00:24:30.700 --> 00:24:31.100
Preview
The Masked Actress

00:24:31.100 --> 00:24:34.840
Preview
It looks like Yumi-san will also have a
different kind of painful experience.
The Masked Actress

00:24:34.840 --> 00:24:35.890
Preview
The Masked Actress
